Protection and Control / Electrical Engineer$80,000 to $130,000 base + Annual BonusRemote
Are you an electrical engineer with protection and control experience? Currently working in the utilities industry and are open for a change? Looking for a company which has grown adding employee's year on year?
The client I'm working with has found a niche service offering within electrical protection and controls, they're looking to add to their team with engineers who have experience in implementing and servicing microprocessors for electrical systems.
The RoleAs an Electrical Engineer, you can expect the following;
ø Working closely with clients to understand project requirements and solutions.ø Troubleshooting and diagnosing microprocessors.ø Implementing new and servicing original relay protectors.ø Utilizing ETAP.
Ideal CandidateTo be considered for the Electrical Engineer role, we are looking for the following;
ø Prior experience working with a range of voltages ranging from 120kV to 335kV.ø Working experience with ETAP or ASPEN.ø Previously background in protection and control, or utilities.ø Completed projects where you have had to design aspects of electrical systems previously.
The PackageThe client I'm working with is offering a great salary and benefits package including;
ø Base salary between $80,000 to $130,000.ø Annual bonus based on personal and company performance, along with O/T paid for.ø 100% healthcare covered.
